A||||1||turbo86se||replacing '88 front control arm||||1||
Z||000000||turbo86se||10-20-2001||01:01 PM||||Hi everyone, <BR>I'm considering buying a white '88 coupe that has been sitting for a while at a local wrecking yard. It's in real good shape except for when the owner slammed it into a ditch. The front left wheel is sitting back towards the middle of the car and angled in. If I were to get the Fiero, how hard is it to remove the front control arm and whatever else may be bad? Is this something the do-it-yourselfer can do in their driveway? <BR>I've got several pics of the car, but I still can't figure out the PIP yet. So I could email them to someone for posting. <BR>TIA!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-20-2001||04:00 PM||||It is very simple.....especially if it is the upper control arm.  I have removed the upper control arms off of '88 Fieros with them still on the ground and wheels attached!  All it takes is a 15mm socket, a ratchet (or breaker bar) and a hammer.  <P>Remove the 15mm nut that holds the upper balljoint to the spindle.  Now start loosening the two 15 mm bolts that attach the control arm to the frame crossmember.  There is a nut plate on the underside that occasionally breaks free, so be aware of that.  If the bolts don't seem to be loosening, but spin freely then the nutplates are probably busted.  You will need a 18 or 19mm (can't remember which) box end wrench to hold the nut in place while you continue to remove the bolts.<P>Once the two bolts are loose/off, whack the balljoint stud with the hammer until it pops off.  Voila!  You're done.<P>Now, depending on how hard it hit the ditch, you may also need to replace the lower control arm, spindle or even the entire crossmember itself.  Carefully inspect everything under the left front end and replace whatever looks funny.<P>The lower control arm is a very sturdy piece of metal, so it is likely not bent, but you never know.  I have seen the crossmember flanges (where the lower control arm attaches) bend in a wreck, but the control arm itself was still straight. <P>E-mail me if you need any other help with this.  I also have some '88 suspension parts, if you need them.<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
